  "body": "## Scope and dependency\n\nDepends on draft #403 (`6047377348e901c919d7691b849faab30980b952`); do not merge independently.\n\nAdds one private SQL command to complete opted-in preparation tasks in draft/planning events. Reuses canonical logistics activities, dependencies, scoped authority, RACI, task write fences, aggregate revisions, immutable audit and command receipts. No new table or second task domain. This is not yet a public API or UI workflow.\n\n## Requirements and invariants\n\nTC01\u201307 / EO-023, EO-026\u2013028, EO-045, EO-051, EO-055\u2013058: current scoped authority after blocking locks, exact target and revision, completed prerequisites, exactly one current Accountable and at least one current Responsible, task/operation-scoped idempotency, atomic status/version/audit/receipt effects. No dependency override path. Same-content historical replay requires current read access; revoked or hidden targets disclose no receipt.\n\n## Formal and executed verification\n\nFormal specification and the full pinned suite passed before feature SQL: 24 positive TLC configurations, 60 named negative controls, 13 PlusCal integrity tests, 2 SAT Alloy scenarios and 13 UNSAT assertions. New model: 944,014 generated / 231,576 distinct states, depth 14; seven intended counterexamples detected. These are bounded checks, not an unbounded proof or proof of SQL refinement.\n\nExecuted locally:\n\n- `sh scripts/test-event-task-completion-migration.sh`: PASS, including 32 decision cases, rejected/private inputs, history/retries, injected persistence faults, overflow/outer rollback, down/up, 12 observed two-writer races across RC/RR/SERIALIZABLE, four expiry waits, revocation ordering and aborted-first recovery.\n- `bash scripts/test-event-operations-schema-rehearsal.sh`: PASS on the authoritative complete schema, including new command assertions, constraint validation, rollback/reapply and final schema verification. No diagnostic workaround.\n- Combined runner/schema/RACI/CI Node tests: 36/36 PASS; shell syntax, workflow YAML parsing and diff whitespace checks passed.\n\nAn intermediate expiry test failed because a four-second grant expired before the command started. Coordinator setup now precedes a 15-second window; valid start, exact blocking PID, real expiry and rejection remain required. The full rerun passed. No test was waived. Disposable DB containers had no network or published ports, were removed, and diagnostic logs retained.\n\nNo new Haskell/UI/mobile build or browser run; public contracts and generated clients unchanged. Hosted CI for this head is pending and is not inferred from parent/local results. Existing catalog governance backlog remains unwaived.\n\n## Security, schema and rollback\n\nSECURITY INVOKER, fixed search path, no PUBLIC execution, existing feature flag required. Not included in the production migration manifest. SQL actor arguments are not authentication: a future HTTP change must compose the existing session fence and validate the receipt before COMMIT.\n\nMigration only creates the private function; rollback only drops it. Never reopen tasks, reset versions or erase accepted receipts/audit. Reapply preserves keys. Quiesce future callers before rollback; no caller is exposed here. No production activation, deployment, provider or real-money action.\n\n## Remaining work and detailed evidence\n\nHTTP/client/UI, evidence and approver workflows, authorized overrides, reopening, live-event effects, notifications, native mobile and durable offline recovery remain dependent work. The complete event-operations mission is not done.\n\n[Contract, exact formal command and bounds](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/feat/event-task-completion-command/docs/event-operations/task-completion-contract.md)\n\n[Full implementation and verification report](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/feat/event-task-completion-command/docs/event-operations/pr-31-task-completion-command.md)\n",
